        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e1d1fd91-53c0-5781-acb5-7102101cafd7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg\n- People: Bonne de Luxembourg, John the Blind, John II of France, Jean Le Noir\n- Places: The Cloisters, New York\n- Topics: illuminated manuscripts\n\nFacts:\n- John the Blind was born on 10 August 1296, became Count of Luxembourg in 1309, became King of Bohemia in 1310, and was also titular King of Poland.\n- John the Blind died on 26 August 1346.\n- The Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg is a small 14th-century illuminated manuscript made in tempera, grisaille, ink, and gold leaf on vellum.\n- The Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg was probably executed for Bonne de Luxembourg, Duchess of Normandy, who was the daughter of John the Blind and the wife of John II of France.\n- The Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg was probably made around 1348–1349, likely near the end of John II of France's life.\n- Jean Le Noir's main work is the Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg, dated about 1348–1349.\n- The Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg is now in the collection of The Cloisters in New York.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "da637ea2-6d46-56a9-968c-411be70c72be",
        "text": "Page: Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg. Sentence: The Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg is a small 14th-century illuminated manuscript in tempera, grisaille, ink and gold leaf on vellum, now in the collection of The Cloisters, New York.\nPage: Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg. Sentence: It was probably executed for Bonne de Luxembourg, Duchess of Normandy, daughter of John the Blind and the wife of John II of France, probably at the end of her husband's life, c 1348-49.\nPage: John of Bohemia. Sentence: John the Blind (Luxembourgish: \"Jang de Blannen\" ; German: \"Johann der Blinde von Luxemburg\" ; ; 10 August 1296 – 26 August 1346) was the Count of Luxembourg from 1309 and King of Bohemia from 1310 and titular King of Poland.\nPage: Jean Le Noir (illuminator). Sentence: His main work is the \"Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg\" (c. 1348-1349, New York, The Cloisters, Inv.",
